## Range-based `for` loops
C-style iteration over arrays and containers is prone to indexing errors and is also tedious to type. To eliminate these
errors, and make your code more readable, use range-based `for` loops with both Standard Library containers and raw
arrays. For more information, see Range-based `for` statement.
